  13               Stage B: rx_is_bus_reset()        (decoder -- reset detect)
  14               Stage C: rx_pesec_correct()       (ecc -- 26-bit SEC+DED)
  15               Stage D: rx_process_bus_state()   (decoder -- absolute nibble decode + FSM)
  16          
  17             The previous Stage D (rx_correct_bus_state, H1 differential validation)
  18             was removed per design directive.  Nibble extraction in the new Stage D
  19             relies on the TX invariant
  20                  syndrome(current_bus_state) == last_input_nibble
  21             so the absolute syndrome of the PESEC-corrected data is itself the
  22             recovered nibble -- no "previous bus state" anchor needs to be
  23             maintained, and no resynchronisation handshake is required after a
  24             dropped frame.  Byte-boundary alignment in the FSM is handled
  25             independently by rx_skip_next_frame in rx_decoder.c.
